IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `or336-nouns`
IMPORT `or336-art336`
IMPORT `or336-art336a`
IMPORT `or336-art336b`

-- Art. 336, 336a and 336b of the Swiss Code of Obligations (OR, SR 220):
-- abusive termination of an employment contract, Fedlex consolidated version
-- applicable from 2026-10-01, in German -- THE EMPLOYEE'S SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the employee (one person, in one employment with one employer), asking
-- on facts they can state whether a notice of termination, given by their
-- employer or by themselves, is abusive; what they can claim, and how much at
-- most; and by when they must object and bring their action to keep a claim.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above as the
-- questions an employee would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no layer-1
-- rule is restated: each question builds the records the rules read from plain
-- inputs and calls the rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a date, a number, a
-- choice from a list), one for each fact the employee states, each with an
-- @desc worded as the employee would be asked. The text is German; every
-- question, input name and description here is the encoder's English gloss,
-- with the German term of art beside it.
--
-- Facts a rule does not read in a question are given a fixed placeholder, with
-- a comment saying why. The facts about the grounds are asked from the position
-- of "the person who received the notice" (the text's "die andere Partei"),
-- and each description says who that is for the employee.
--
-- WHAT A RESULT MEANS. Questions that answer yes or no return JUST TRUE (the
-- text's condition is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words: see
-- the header of or336-art336.l4) or NOTHING (the text does not decide: its own
-- wording limits the provision and the case falls outside the limit). A
-- caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. For Art 336 as a whole, JUST
-- FALSE means that no listed ground is met on these facts; it does not say
-- that no other ground exists, because the text does not say that its list is
-- closed. The amount of the compensation is for the judge: only its ceiling
-- (the cap of six months' wages, two months' wages for the mass-dismissal
-- ground) is answered, from the monthly wage the employee states.
--
-- Where this layer departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded, not
-- hidden): the questions are asked of a notice that may have been given by
-- either party, because Art 336(1) speaks of "eine Partei"; judgments the text
-- leaves to the person (a characteristic's connection with the employment, a
-- justified reason, good faith, a mass dismissal, consultation) are plain
-- facts; the notice period and the day the employment ends are dates the
-- employee states, because the text names no rule for them.
-- The employer's seat is a separate layer beside this one,
-- or336-seat-employer.l4, over the same modules.

§ `Art 336 to 336b OR -- the employee's questions`

§§ `Is the notice abusive?`

-- Art. 336. Asked of a notice you received or a notice you gave. The questions about the employer's notice (Art 336(2) and (3)) arise only if your employer gave you notice: the form can ask "Has your employer given you notice?" first.

-- Art 336(1)(a). A notice, from either party, is abusive if it is given because of a characteristic that the other party holds by virtue of personality, unless the characteristic is connected with the employment or substantially impairs cooperation in the business.
@export Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive because of a personal characteristic (Art 336(1)(a))` IS
    `Art 336(1)(a) the notice is abusive` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`

-- Art 336(1)(b). A notice, from either party, is abusive if it is given because the other party exercises a constitutional right, unless the exercise breaches a duty from the employment or substantially impairs cooperation in the business.
@export Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive because a constitutional right was exercised (Art 336(1)(b))` IS
    `Art 336(1)(b) the notice is abusive` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`

-- Art 336(1)(c). A notice, from either party, is abusive if it is given exclusively to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment.
@export Is the notice abusive because it was given only to thwart claims (Art 336(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive because it was given only to thwart claims (Art 336(1)(c))` IS
    `Art 336(1)(c) the notice is abusive` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`

-- Art 336(1)(d). A notice, from either party, is abusive if it is given because the other party asserts claims from the employment in good faith.
@export Is the notice abusive because claims were asserted in good faith (Art 336(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive because claims were asserted in good faith (Art 336(1)(d))` IS
    `Art 336(1)(d) the notice is abusive` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`

-- Art 336(1)(e). A notice, from either party, is abusive if it is given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military or civil protection service or Swiss civilian service, or fulfils a legal duty it did not take on voluntarily.
@export Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive because of service or a legal duty (Art 336(1)(e))` IS
    `Art 336(1)(e) the notice is abusive` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`

-- Art 336(2)(a). A notice given by the employer is, in addition, abusive if it is given because the employee belongs, or does not belong, to an employees' association, or lawfully takes part in union activity. This is asked only of a notice given by the employer ("Has your employer given you notice?").
@export Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my employer gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give the notice? Answer yes if your employer ended your employment by notice, and no if you gave the notice.
      `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you belong to an employees' association (Arbeitnehmerverband)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you do not belong to an employees' association?
      `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you lawfully take part in union activity (gewerkschaftliche Tätigkeit)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's notice abusive because of my union membership or activity (Art 336(2)(a))` IS
    `Art 336(2)(a) the notice is abusive` `the party giving notice` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS
            IF `my employer gave the notice` THEN Employer ELSE Employee
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity`

-- Art 336(2)(b) and (3). A notice given by the employer is, in addition, abusive if it is given while the employee is an elected employee representative and the employer cannot prove a justified reason; after a transfer the protection lasts as long as the mandate would have lasted. This is asked only of a notice given by the employer.
@export Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))?
GIVEN `my employer gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give the notice? Answer yes if your employer ended your employment by notice, and no if you gave the notice.
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in a body of the business (betriebliche Einrichtung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in an institution connected with the undertaking (dem Unternehmen angeschlossene Einrichtung)?
      `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your employer prove that it had a justified reason (begründeter Anlass) for the notice?
      `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your mandate as employee representative end because the employment was transferred to a new employer (Art. 333)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
      `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day would your mandate as employee representative have ended if the employment had not been transferred? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's notice abusive because I am an elected employee representative (Art 336(2)(b) and (3))` IS
    `Art 336(2)(b) the notice is abusive` `the party giving notice` `my facts` `my facts about the transfer`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS
            IF `my employer gave the notice` THEN Employer ELSE Employee
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business`
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking`
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice`
        `my facts about the transfer` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred`
            `the day the notice was given` IS `the day the notice was given`
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred`

-- Art 336(2)(c). A notice given by the employer is, in addition, abusive if it is given as part of a mass dismissal without the employee representation (or, if there is none, the employees) having been consulted. This is asked only of a notice given by the employer.
@export Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my employer gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give the notice? Answer yes if your employer ended your employment by notice, and no if you gave the notice.
      `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given as part of a mass dismissal (Massenentlassung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the employees have an employee representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the employees have an employee representation (Arbeitnehmervertretung)?
      `the employee representation was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee representation consulted before the notices were given?
      `the employees were consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the employees themselves consulted before the notices were given? (This matters only where there is no employee representation.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's notice abusive because it was part of a mass dismissal without consultation (Art 336(2)(c))` IS
    `Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` `the party giving notice` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS
            IF `my employer gave the notice` THEN Employer ELSE Employee
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal`
            `there is an employee representation` IS `the employees have an employee representation`
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS `the employee representation was consulted`
            `the employees were consulted` IS `the employees were consulted`

-- Art 336 as a whole. A notice is abusive on a ground the Article lists if any ground of paragraph 1 is met (either party's notice) or, for a notice given by the employer, any ground of paragraph 2 or 3. JUST FALSE means that no listed ground is met on these facts; it does not say that no other ground exists, because the text does not say that its list is closed.
@export Is the notice abusive on a ground Art 336 lists?
GIVEN `my employer gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give the notice? Answer yes if your employer ended your employment by notice, and no if you gave the notice.
      `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
      `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you belong to an employees' association (Arbeitnehmerverband)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you do not belong to an employees' association?
      `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you lawfully take part in union activity (gewerkschaftliche Tätigkeit)?
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in a body of the business (betriebliche Einrichtung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in an institution connected with the undertaking (dem Unternehmen angeschlossene Einrichtung)?
      `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your employer prove that it had a justified reason (begründeter Anlass) for the notice?
      `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your mandate as employee representative end because the employment was transferred to a new employer (Art. 333)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
      `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day would your mandate as employee representative have ended if the employment had not been transferred? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
      `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given as part of a mass dismissal (Massenentlassung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the employees have an employee representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the employees have an employee representation (Arbeitnehmervertretung)?
      `the employee representation was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee representation consulted before the notices were given?
      `the employees were consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the employees themselves consulted before the notices were given? (This matters only where there is no employee representation.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice abusive on a ground Art 336 lists` IS
    `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS
            IF `my employer gave the notice` THEN Employer ELSE Employee
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business`
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking`
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal`
            `there is an employee representation` IS `the employees have an employee representation`
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS `the employee representation was consulted`
            `the employees were consulted` IS `the employees were consulted`
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred`
            `the day the notice was given` IS `the day the notice was given`
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred`
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS `the party giving notice`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`

§§ `What can I claim, and what could I owe?`

-- Art. 336a. These arise only if the notice may be abusive: the form can ask "Do you think the notice was abusive?" first.

-- Art 336a(1). The party that gives an abusive notice owes the other party a compensation. Asked for a notice your employer gave you; the answer is NOTHING where no listed ground is met, because the text speaks only of an abusive notice.
@export Am I owed compensation for the notice my employer gave me (Art 336a(1))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
      `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you belong to an employees' association (Arbeitnehmerverband)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you do not belong to an employees' association?
      `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because you lawfully take part in union activity (gewerkschaftliche Tätigkeit)?
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in a body of the business (betriebliche Einrichtung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given while you were an elected employee representative in an institution connected with the undertaking (dem Unternehmen angeschlossene Einrichtung)?
      `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your employer prove that it had a justified reason (begründeter Anlass) for the notice?
      `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your mandate as employee representative end because the employment was transferred to a new employer (Art. 333)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
      `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day would your mandate as employee representative have ended if the employment had not been transferred? (Any date if the employment was not transferred.)
      `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given as part of a mass dismissal (Massenentlassung)? Only a notice given by the employer is read under this question.
      `the employees have an employee representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the employees have an employee representation (Arbeitnehmervertretung)?
      `the employee representation was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employee representation consulted before the notices were given?
      `the employees were consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the employees themselves consulted before the notices were given? (This matters only where there is no employee representation.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed compensation for the notice my employer gave me (Art 336a(1))` IS
    `Art 336a(1) the party giving notice owes the other party compensation`
        (`Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`)
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS Employer
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association`
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS `the notice was given because the employee lawfully takes part in union activity`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business`
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking`
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS `the employer can prove it had a justified reason for the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal`
            `there is an employee representation` IS `the employees have an employee representation`
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS `the employee representation was consulted`
            `the employees were consulted` IS `the employees were consulted`
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS `the employee's mandate as representative ended because the employment was transferred`
            `the day the notice was given` IS `the day the notice was given`
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS `the last day the employee's mandate would have lasted if the employment had not been transferred`
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS Employer
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`

