            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`

-- Art 336a(2). The compensation may not exceed the employee's wages for six months; the judge fixes the amount.
@export What is the most I can be made to pay my employer for the notice I gave (Art 336a(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because of a characteristic that the person who received it holds by virtue of their personality (Persönlichkeit)? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `that characteristic is connected with the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that characteristic connected with the employment relationship?
      `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that characteristic substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right breach a duty arising from the employment relationship?
      `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did exercising that right substantially impair cooperation in the business?
      `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given in order to prevent claims of the person who received it from the employment from arising? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was thwarting those claims the only purpose of the notice, with no other purpose beside it?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice assert those claims in good faith (nach Treu und Glauben)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service? (If your employer gave you notice, that person is you; if you gave the notice, it is your employer.)
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service (Schutzdienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service (Zivildienst)?
      `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty (gesetzliche Pflicht)?
      `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who received the notice take on that legal duty voluntarily (freiwillig übernommen)?
      `my wages for one month` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your wages for one month? (Give every amount in the same currency.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be made to pay my employer for the notice I gave (Art 336a(2) and (3))` IS
    `Art 336a(2) and (3) the most the compensation can be`
        `abusive on a listed ground`
        (`Art 336(2)(c) the notice is abusive` `the party giving notice` `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`)
        `my wages for one month`
    WHERE
        `the party giving notice` MEANS Employee
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(a) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because of a characteristic the other party holds by virtue of personality` IS `the notice was given because of a personal characteristic of the person who received it`
            `the characteristic is connected with the employment` IS `that characteristic is connected with the employment`
            `the characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `that characteristic substantially impairs cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party exercises a constitutional right` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it exercised a constitutional right`
            `the exercise of the right breaches a duty from the employment` IS `exercising that right breached a duty from the employment`
            `the exercise of the right substantially impairs cooperation in the business` IS `exercising that right substantially impaired cooperation in the business`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(c) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given to thwart the arising of the other party's claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given to thwart claims the person who received it would have had from the employment`
            `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice` IS `thwarting those claims was the only purpose of the notice`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(d) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party asserts claims from the employment` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it asserted claims from the employment`
            `the other party asserts those claims in good faith` IS `the person who received the notice asserted those claims in good faith`
        `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)` MEANS `Art 336(1)(e) facts` WITH
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory military service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory military service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss compulsory civil protection service`
            `the notice was given because the other party performs Swiss civilian service` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it performs Swiss civilian service`
            `the notice was given because the other party fulfils a legal duty` IS `the notice was given because the person who received it is fulfilling a legal duty`
            `the other party assumed that legal duty voluntarily` IS `the person who received the notice took on that legal duty voluntarily`
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(a) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given because the employee belongs to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee does not belong to an employees' association` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given because the employee lawfully exercises a union activity` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(b) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body of the business` IS FALSE
            `the notice was given while the employee was an elected employee representative in a body connected with the undertaking` IS FALSE
            `the employer can prove a justified reason for the notice` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)` MEANS `Art 336(2)(c) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the notice was given as part of a mass dismissal` IS FALSE
            `there is an employee representation` IS FALSE
            `the employee representation was consulted` IS FALSE
            `the employees were consulted` IS FALSE
        `my facts for Art 336(3)` MEANS `Art 336(3) facts` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the notice was given by the employee, and Art. 336(2) and (3) speak only of a notice given by the employer, so these facts are not read.
            `the mandate ended because the employment was transferred` IS FALSE
            `the day the notice was given` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the last day the mandate would have lasted had the employment not been transferred` IS Date 1 1 2000
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of termination` WITH
            `given by` IS Employee
            `facts for Art 336(1)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(d)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(d)`
            `facts for Art 336(1)(e)` IS `my facts for Art 336(1)(e)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(a)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(a)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(b)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(b)`
            `facts for Art 336(2)(c)` IS `my facts for Art 336(2)(c)`
            `facts for Art 336(3)` IS `my facts for Art 336(3)`
        `abusive on a listed ground` MEANS
            `Art 336 a ground the Article lists makes the notice abusive` `my notice`

-- Art 336a(2). The cap applies to the compensation; damages claims on another legal basis are reserved.
@export Does the cap on compensation apply to my claim (Art 336a(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What kind of claim is it? Choose one of: compensation under Art 336a; damages on another legal basis; another kind of claim.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the cap on compensation apply to my claim (Art 336a(2))` IS
    `Art 336a(2) the cap limits this claim` `the kind of claim`

§§ `Keeping a claim: the objection and the action`

-- Art. 336b. These arise only for a person who received a notice and wants to claim the compensation: the form can ask "Do you want to claim compensation for the notice?" first.

-- Art 336b(1). Whoever wants to assert the compensation must object to the notice in writing, with the party that gave it, at the latest by the end of the notice period. Asked of you as the party that received the notice.
@export Is my objection to the notice valid (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `my objection was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to the notice in writing?
      `my objection was directed against the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `my objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the objection to the party that gave the notice (your employer, if your employer gave it)?
      `the day my objection was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the objection?
      `the last day of my notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my objection to the notice valid (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `my objection was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `my objection was directed against the notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `my objection was made to the party that gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day my objection was made`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of my notice period`

-- Art 336b(1). The objection must be made at the latest by the end of the notice period.
@export What is the last day I can object to the notice (Art 336b(1))?
GIVEN `the last day of my notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can object to the notice (Art 336b(1))` IS
    `Art 336b(1) the last day to object` `the last day of my notice period`

-- Art 336b(2), first sentence. If the objection was valid and the parties do not agree on continuing the employment, the party that received the notice can assert the claim.
@export Can I assert my claim for compensation (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `my objection was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to the notice in writing?
      `my objection was directed against the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your objection directed against the notice of termination itself?
      `my objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the objection to the party that gave the notice (your employer, if your employer gave it)?
      `the day my objection was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the objection?
      `the last day of my notice period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your notice period end? (The last day of the notice period.)
      `we agreed on continuing the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the party that gave the notice agree on continuing the employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I assert my claim for compensation (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the party that received the notice can assert the compensation claim`
        (`Art 336b(1) the objection meets the requirements` `my objection`)
        `we agreed on continuing the employment`
    WHERE
        `my objection` MEANS `Objection` WITH
            -- Fixed: this question is about the compensation of Art. 336 and 336a, so the claim rests on them.
            `the claim rests on Art 336 and 336a` IS TRUE
            `the objection was made in writing` IS `my objection was made in writing`
            `the objection was directed against the notice` IS `my objection was directed against the notice`
            `the objection was made to the party that gave the notice` IS `my objection was made to the party that gave the notice`
            `the day the objection was made` IS `the day my objection was made`
            `the last day of the notice period` IS `the last day of my notice period`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence. An action has to be made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment.
@export What is the last day I can bring my action (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, your employment end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can bring my action (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the last day to bring the action` `the day my employment ended`

-- Art 336b(2), second sentence. If no action is made pending within 180 days after the end of the employment, the claim is forfeited.
@export Has my claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))?
GIVEN `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did, or will, your employment end?
      `I have brought an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you brought an action in court on the claim (an action made pending, anhängig gemacht)?
      `the day I brought the action` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you bring the action? (Any date if you have not brought one.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know the position of your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my claim been forfeited (Art 336b(2))` IS
    `Art 336b(2) the claim is forfeited` `my action`
    WHERE
        `my action` MEANS `Action on the claim` WITH
            `the day the employment ended` IS `the day my employment ended`
            `an action has been brought` IS `I have brought an action`
            `the day the action was brought` IS `the day I brought the action`
            `the day asked about` IS `the day I am asking about`
